WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.962
A memory the same size at token ten and at token one million.

00:00:03.962 --> 00:00:05.559
What does it have to forget?

00:00:10.377 --> 00:00:11.289
Hi, I'm Ripley!

00:00:11.289 --> 00:00:15.543
This is the layer that fills three slots in four of Qwen's recent models.

00:00:19.142 --> 00:00:20.267
Sixty-four layers.

00:00:22.142 --> 00:00:24.009
Forty-eight keep a fixed memory.

00:00:24.009 --> 00:00:28.116
Sixteen are ordinary attention, and their cache grows with every token.

00:00:29.983 --> 00:00:32.086
Each head keeps one matrix, the state.

00:00:32.086 --> 00:00:33.288
Every token edits it.

00:00:33.708 --> 00:00:35.244
Alpha decays the whole state.

00:00:35.244 --> 00:00:37.087
Near zero, it wipes the memory.

00:00:37.507 --> 00:00:40.566
Then it reads what the state holds for this key, and takes it out.

00:00:40.986 --> 00:00:43.045
And writes the new value in its place.

00:00:43.045 --> 00:00:44.074
Beta sets how hard.

00:00:45.975 --> 00:00:47.624
Follow one token through one head.

00:00:47.624 --> 00:00:50.646
It brings a query, a key, a value and two gates.

00:00:51.046 --> 00:00:51.971
First the decay.

00:00:53.646 --> 00:00:54.540
Then the erase.

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:57.817
A repeated key replaces its value instead of blending with it.

00:00:58.217 --> 00:00:58.998
Then the write.

00:01:00.817 --> 00:01:03.205
The query reads the result with one product.

00:01:03.205 --> 00:01:04.698
Same cost at any length.

00:01:06.367 --> 00:01:07.181
The paper's block.

00:01:07.181 --> 00:01:10.439
Short convolutions on the query, key and value, a norm on the

00:01:10.439 --> 00:01:12.339
keys, and a gate on the output.

00:01:12.719 --> 00:01:15.822
Its hybrids paired the layer with windowed attention.

00:01:15.822 --> 00:01:18.149
Production models chose full attention instead.

00:01:19.833 --> 00:01:24.201
So a block is three recurrent layers and one attention layer, sixteen times over.

00:01:24.621 --> 00:01:27.323
Only the attention layer keeps a cache that grows.

00:01:27.323 --> 00:01:29.725
It does the exact lookups a summary cannot.

00:01:31.517 --> 00:01:36.161
One layer in four stays global, because a finite state cannot reproduce

00:01:36.161 --> 00:01:40.031
exact token-level retrieval no matter how well it is gated.

00:01:41.758 --> 00:01:47.033
At a quarter of a million tokens, the sixteen attention layers hold seventeen gigabytes.

00:01:47.033 --> 00:01:49.294
All sixty-four would hold almost seventy.

00:01:50.425 --> 00:01:52.505
The fixed part is small, and fragile.

00:01:52.505 --> 00:01:55.773
Store it in sixteen-bit floats and the score falls fifteen points.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:00.474
Three layers keep a cheap memory they can edit.

00:02:00.474 --> 00:02:02.710
The fourth keeps everything, for exact recall.

00:02:04.733 --> 00:02:07.868
Decay, erase, write, and one attention layer in four.

00:02:07.868 --> 00:02:08.914
Thanks for watching!

00:02:09.334 --> 00:02:11.411
Every source is in the full article.

00:02:11.411 --> 00:02:12.004
I'm Ripley.

00:02:12.004 --> 00:02:12.301
Bye!
